speechtext:
No, it is a part of the over-all study. We have not had the final report on the whole basin of the Columbia river. I believe the hon. member for Vancouver-Quadra might be interested to know how the studies are proceeding and how far we have reached, if I could give him the figures:
The mapping is 100 per cent completed;
River reconnaissance surveys, 100 per cent;
Dam site investigations, 95 per cent;
Flowage surveys, 75 per cent;
Irrigation surveys, 90 per cent;
Soil surveys, 100 per cent;
Other ancillary investigations and reports, 40 per cent;
Office studies, 60 per cent;
Design of works, 60 per cent.
